对。

492
00:22:02.530 --> 00:22:04.310
You guys play like three times a week, right?
你们这群人一周大概打三次球，对吧？

493
00:22:04.310 --> 00:22:04.930
Yeah.
对。

494
00:22:05.210 --> 00:22:09.030
I mean, we are traveling here and there, so we have other people that fill in.
我的意思是，我们到处飞来飞去，所以会有其他人来替补。

495
00:22:09.110 --> 00:22:12.490
We also have a Sunday group that's amazing, Debbie and Francette and Julie.
我们还有一个超棒的主日小组，有黛比、弗兰谢特和朱莉。

496
00:22:12.770 --> 00:22:16.330
But my regular game is with April, Rebecca, and Betsy.
但我固定的球局是和阿普丽尔、丽贝卡还有贝茜一起打。

497
00:22:16.470 --> 00:22:21.390
And I gave you their information, and I'm a little scared.
我把她们的联系方式交给你了，而我有点害怕。

498
00:22:22.150 --> 00:22:25.350
Well, I reached out to these ladies, and here's what I asked them.
好吧，我联系了这些女士，我问了她们这样一个问题。

499
00:22:25.730 --> 00:22:30.550
I said, Angela has told me that she has a whole other side to her that I don't know,
我说，安杰拉告诉我，她有着我所不了解的另一面，

500
00:22:30.890 --> 00:22:33.950
that it's a competitive side that comes out when she plays tennis,
那是一种在她打网球时才会展现出来的争强好胜的一面，

501
00:22:34.130 --> 00:22:36.470
and that you all have nicknames for her.
你们还都给她起了外号。

502
00:22:36.910 --> 00:22:37.810
Oh, gosh.
天哪。

503
00:22:37.930 --> 00:22:41.190
She has given me permission to do a little digging, and I was wondering
她允许我做了一点小调查，我想知道

504
00:22:41.190 --> 00:22:45.870
if you could share a little bit about this other Angela that I don't know.
你们能不能跟我分享一点关于我所不知道的另一个安吉拉的事。

505
00:22:46.170 --> 00:22:48.130
Oh, lady, they had fun with this.
天哪，姑娘，她们在这上面玩得很开心。

506
00:22:48.770 --> 00:22:50.970
They got together, the three of them.
她们聚在一起，她们三个。

507
00:22:50.970 --> 00:22:52.030
Oh, my gosh.
我的天哪。

508
00:22:52.350 --> 00:22:53.690
Betsy's in England.
贝茜在英国。

509
00:22:53.690 --> 00:22:58.890
They got together on a Zoom, and they recorded this message for you.
她们通过 Zoom 聚在一起，为这段录音给你留了话。

510
00:22:58.990 --> 00:23:01.690
I was laughing so hard the whole time I was listening to this.
我听这段的时候全程笑得不行。

511
00:23:02.190 --> 00:23:07.970
So, okay, first of all, let's listen to how they described your tennis alter ego.
所以，好吧，首先，让我们听听她们是怎么描述你的网球分身。

512
00:23:08.750 --> 00:23:15.270
Okay, so we're here to talk about our friend Angela and her tennis life, which is rich.
好，我们来聊聊我们的朋友安吉拉和她的网球生活，非常丰富。

513
00:23:15.570 --> 00:23:18.770
She basically, her whole life revolves around that.
基本上，她的整个生活都围绕着这个转。

514
00:23:18.770 --> 00:23:22.290
I mean, her kids, obviously, Josh, but the podcast, but it's mostly tennis.
我是说，她的孩子们，当然还有乔什，还有播客，但主要还是网球。

515
00:23:22.470 --> 00:23:24.210
If she could have her way, it would just be tennis.
如果由她做主，那就只有网球了。

516
00:23:24.530 --> 00:23:25.330
Wouldn't you say?
你说是吧？

517
00:23:25.770 --> 00:23:26.110
Yes.
对。

518
00:23:26.650 --> 00:23:27.090
Absolutely.
绝对的。

519
00:23:27.310 --> 00:23:27.830
Totally agree.
完全同意。

520
00:23:28.050 --> 00:23:28.290
Yes.
是的。

521
00:23:28.550 --> 00:23:32.190
And, you know, I think you put it really well, April.
而且，你知道，我觉得你总结得很好，埃普丽尔。

522
00:23:32.530 --> 00:23:36.030
There's a side of Angela you don't know unless you play tennis with her.
安吉拉有一面，除非你跟她打网球，否则你是不会了解的。

523
00:23:36.870 --> 00:23:38.330
Well, yeah, that's right.
嗯，对，没错。

524
00:23:38.570 --> 00:23:44.150
So she'll show up to play tennis in the Angela that we all know and love, right?
所以她来打网球时，会展现出我们都熟悉且热爱的那个安吉拉，对吧？

525
00:23:44.250 --> 00:23:51.470
Where she, like, arrives and she has, like, a granola from Josh and some little gift for us and some sweet story.
她到场时，会带着乔什做的燕麦棒，给我们带点小礼物，还有一些温馨的故事。

526
00:23:51.710 --> 00:23:52.610
And she's, like...
然后她会说……

527
00:23:52.610 --> 00:23:53.990
She's sure it's made for everybody.
她确信这是给大家准备的。

528
00:23:54.310 --> 00:23:59.750
She's sure she brought me a hummingbird feeder and, like, you know, like, all these beautiful things.
她确信她给我带来了蜂鸟喂食器，还有，你知道的，诸如此类所有美好的东西。

529
00:23:59.990 --> 00:24:01.410
Here's the new tea I have.
这是我新买的茶。

530
00:24:01.510 --> 00:24:02.570
You have to try it.
你们必须尝尝。

531
00:24:02.870 --> 00:24:05.170
The most considerate person ever.
最体贴的人没有之一。

532
00:24:05.330 --> 00:24:05.830
Oh, considerate.
哦，体贴。

533
00:24:05.910 --> 00:24:06.090
Yes.
是的。

534
00:24:06.290 --> 00:24:09.230
Literally, like, the kindest, sweetest, most considerate.
简直就是，最善良、最甜美、最体贴。

535
00:24:09.330 --> 00:24:10.830
And then we get on the court, right?
然后我们上了球场，对吧？

536
00:24:11.810 --> 00:24:12.210
Yeah.
对。

537
00:24:12.210 --> 00:24:12.870
She's like the Hulk.
她就像绿巨人。

538
00:24:15.470 --> 00:24:16.610
She is.
她确实是。

539
00:24:16.790 --> 00:24:18.650
There's a Jekyll and Hyde.
简直是杰基尔和海德的双重人格。

540
00:24:18.990 --> 00:24:19.710
Yes.
是的。

541
00:24:20.370 --> 00:24:23.150
But not, like, she's not mean.
但也不是说，她并不刻薄。

542
00:24:23.150 --> 00:24:28.530
She's just really competitive and in cutthroat.
她只是好胜心极强，而且出手狠辣。

543
00:24:28.730 --> 00:24:33.890
So she has this shot and we call it the Angela because it's a really good shot.
所以她有一种击球方式，我们管它叫“安吉拉球”，因为这球打得真好。

544
00:24:34.070 --> 00:24:40.390
She's got a very good forehand and she has this shot where she does a really deep angle.
她的正手非常厉害，她有一种能打出极大角度的击球。

545
00:24:40.390 --> 00:24:43.410
And it's very, very difficult to get to.
而且那个球非常非常难救到。

546
00:24:44.850 --> 00:24:48.570
And, you know, okay, that's fine.
然后，好吧，这倒也没什么。

547
00:24:49.030 --> 00:24:53.410
And the first, like, three times she does it and scores points.
前大概三次她用这招得分。

548
00:24:53.410 --> 00:24:59.350
By the way, when she's up, like, like in the game we play, you know, the winner wins 11.
顺便说一句，当她领先的时候，比如在我们玩的比赛里，你知道的，赢11分制。

549
00:24:59.630 --> 00:25:03.430
Like, when her team is up, like, 7-2, she's still doing that.
比如当她们队以 7 比 2 领先时，她还在用这招。

550
00:25:03.430 --> 00:25:05.150
And that's when I get really mad.
而那就是我真的很生气的时候。

551
00:25:07.570 --> 00:25:09.810
I get mad at, like, three or four, I'll say.
我会生气的，大概在第三个或者第四个球吧，我会这么说。

552
00:25:10.390 --> 00:25:10.610
Yeah.
对。

553
00:25:12.090 --> 00:25:13.230
I'm a little earlier.
我生气的点会稍微早一点。

554
00:25:13.410 --> 00:25:15.190
And I'm actually mad.
而且我是真的生气了。

555
00:25:15.330 --> 00:25:16.650
And I'll go, keep it up.
然后我会说，继续啊。

556
00:25:17.050 --> 00:25:17.990
Keep it up, Angela.
继续啊，安吉拉。

557
00:25:18.370 --> 00:25:19.650
Let's see where that gets you.
我们看你能得意到什么时候。

558
00:25:19.890 --> 00:25:21.350
And I'm so clearly mad.
而且我表现得那么明显。

559
00:25:21.470 --> 00:25:25.150
And she's like, he has no idea that I'm really mad.
而她却觉得，他根本不知道我是真的生气了。

560
00:25:25.310 --> 00:25:27.890
It's like, I'm going to kill you.
那种感觉就像，我要杀了你。

561
00:25:29.630 --> 00:25:34.450
Or the other thing she did to you, Rebecca, the little, like, sometimes she's like a little tip of the hat.
或者她对你做过的另一件事，丽贝卡，就是那种，有时她会像是在向你脱帽致意一样。

562
00:25:34.450 --> 00:25:35.250
And you're like, yeah.
然后你会想，好吧。

563
00:25:35.590 --> 00:25:36.430
Oh, don't do that.
噢，别那样。

564
00:25:36.930 --> 00:25:41.250
It's like she'll do a really wicked shot and then almost curtsy to you.
就好像她打出了一个极其刁钻的球，然后几乎要向你行个屈膝礼。

565
00:25:43.730 --> 00:25:44.310
She does.
她真的会这样。

566
00:25:44.430 --> 00:25:45.550
She has a little leg kick.
她会做一个小小的踢腿动作。

567
00:25:45.710 --> 00:25:47.090
She has a little, like, a leg kick.
她会做一个类似于踢腿的动作。

568
00:25:47.330 --> 00:25:47.550
Yeah.
对。

569
00:25:47.550 --> 00:25:49.630
When you're like, aren't you adorable?
当你会觉得，你难道不是很可爱吗？

570
00:25:51.410 --> 00:25:56.430
We had a fill-in for this woman who is only in town periodically.
我们有个代班的女士，她只是偶尔在镇上待一阵。

571
00:25:56.430 --> 00:25:57.690
And she's Danish.
她是丹麦人。

572
00:25:58.050 --> 00:26:02.210
And she is hilarious because she curses in Danish.
她超级搞笑，因为她会用丹麦语骂人。

573
00:26:04.470 --> 00:26:06.630
And Angela hit two shots back-to-back.
然后安吉拉接连打出了两个精彩的球。

574
00:26:06.830 --> 00:26:07.690
One was in Angla.
一个是压线球。

575
00:26:07.730 --> 00:26:12.370
And then one was this really mean backhand drop shot.
另一个是一个非常狠的反手切削球。

576
00:26:12.670 --> 00:26:14.070
Charlotte cursed at her in Danish.
夏洛特用丹麦语冲她骂了脏话。

577
00:26:14.230 --> 00:26:15.990
And I have no idea what she said.
我完全不知道她说了什么。

578
00:26:16.170 --> 00:26:17.890
And I was on the same side as Charlotte.
当时我和夏洛特在同一边。

579
00:26:18.370 --> 00:26:20.950
And I said, oh, my gosh, I'd love to know what you said.
我说，天哪，我好想知道你刚才说了什么。

580
00:26:21.090 --> 00:26:22.490
And she was like, you really don't want to know.
她就说，你其实并不想知道。

581
00:26:22.770 --> 00:26:23.730
And I was like, it's okay.
我说，没关系的。

582
00:26:24.530 --> 00:26:25.450
I was like, it's okay.
我说，没关系的。

583
00:26:25.450 --> 00:26:27.650
We cursed at her in English all the time.
我们平时也经常用英语骂她。

584
00:26:27.710 --> 00:26:31.270
You can actually tell her what you said.
你其实可以告诉她你刚才说了什么。

585
00:26:32.930 --> 00:26:33.490
Angela.
安吉拉。

586
00:26:36.430 --> 00:26:37.930
Can you see it, Sam?
你能想象到吗，萨姆？

587
00:26:38.170 --> 00:26:40.410
I can absolutely see the curtsying thing.
我完全能想象得出那种行屈膝礼的样子。

588
00:26:40.610 --> 00:26:42.390
I know exactly the leg kick.
我太清楚那个踢腿动作了。

589
00:26:42.550 --> 00:26:43.490
I know the leg kick.
我知道那个踢腿动作。

590
00:26:43.790 --> 00:26:44.130
Yep.
没错。

591
00:26:44.410 --> 00:26:45.110
All of it.
全都能想象到。

592
00:26:46.910 --> 00:26:49.130
But the hulking out, I can't picture.
但是那种暴怒发飙的样子，我实在想象不出来。

593
00:26:49.790 --> 00:26:50.350
What?
什么？

594
00:26:50.530 --> 00:26:55.730
I mean, I'm always like, our purpose is to win, right?
我的意思是，我总是觉得，我们的目标就是赢，对吧？

595
00:26:55.830 --> 00:26:57.050
I'm here to win.
我是来赢的。

596
00:26:57.530 --> 00:26:58.090
Yes.
是的。

597
00:26:58.370 --> 00:27:00.430
So what's the problem?
那有什么问题吗？

598
00:27:04.400 --> 00:27:07.720
Yeah, I think they're looking for like a type of sportsmanship.
对，我觉得他们是在寻找某种体育精神吧。

599
00:27:08.460 --> 00:27:08.940
What?
什么？

600
00:27:09.180 --> 00:27:16.360
Where when you're ahead so far, you know, you do maybe a little bit of what I...
就是当你领先太多的时候，你知道的，你或许会做出一点类似于我...

601
00:27:16.360 --> 00:27:16.960
Take your foot off the gas.
别踩那么猛。

602
00:27:17.140 --> 00:27:17.420
Yeah.
对。

603
00:27:17.640 --> 00:27:20.220
You know, they call it like a gentleman's serve, right?
你知道的，他们管这叫绅士发球，对吧？

604
00:27:20.400 --> 00:27:21.120
Or like a...
或者像...

605
00:27:21.120 --> 00:27:21.380
I know.
我知道。

606
00:27:21.740 --> 00:27:23.520
Sometimes I really do try to do that.
有时我真的会试着那么做。

607
00:27:23.680 --> 00:27:27.120
And then other times you just see the court and you see the shot and you take it.
但有时候你看到球场，看到了机会，就会直接出手。

608
00:27:27.280 --> 00:27:29.640
And you forget that you're up 7-2.
然后你就忘了自己已经以7比2领先了。

609
00:27:29.640 --> 00:27:31.140
You just see the shot.
你只看到了那个球。

610
00:27:31.140 --> 00:27:31.940
So you take it.
所以你就打了。

611
00:27:32.220 --> 00:27:33.200
I think it's fine.
我觉得这挺好的。

612
00:27:33.380 --> 00:27:33.800
You know?
你知道吗？

613
00:27:33.940 --> 00:27:34.820
I'm on your side.
我站你这边。

614
00:27:35.020 --> 00:27:38.560
Listen, you have to know the two people that influenced my tennis career.
听着，你得知道对我的网球生涯产生影响的两个人。

615
00:27:38.900 --> 00:27:42.260
One was Coach Lunn in high school.
一个是高中的兰恩教练。

616
00:27:42.400 --> 00:27:43.340
He coached basketball.
他带的是篮球队。

617
00:27:43.500 --> 00:27:44.720
All he cared about was basketball.
他满脑子只有篮球。

618
00:27:44.940 --> 00:27:48.400
We went to state and we won state for men's basketball.
我们打进了州锦标赛，还拿了男子篮球的州冠军。

619
00:27:48.400 --> 00:27:51.320
So this was a big legacy of his.
所以这是他的一大传奇经历。

620
00:27:51.520 --> 00:27:54.820
And then someone just told him, oh, and you also have to coach tennis.
然后有人突然告诉他，哦，你还得带网球。

621
00:27:55.000 --> 00:27:56.560
And he was probably like, what the hell?
他当时大概心里在想，搞什么鬼？

622
00:27:56.940 --> 00:27:58.000
Because he could give a shit.
因为他根本不在乎。

623
00:27:58.220 --> 00:27:59.440
But he would drive me to matches.
但他会开车送我去比赛。

624
00:27:59.720 --> 00:28:04.840
And right before I left the van to go to my game, as I got out of the van, he'd say,
就在我下车去打比赛前，我刚迈出面包车，他就会说：

625
00:28:04.940 --> 00:28:06.600
Kinsey, victory or death?
金西，不胜则死？

626
00:28:07.120 --> 00:28:07.800
That was it.
就这么简单。

627
00:28:07.960 --> 00:28:09.020
Those are my only options.
这就是我仅有的两个选择。

628
00:28:09.280 --> 00:28:12.300
And then he would nap in the van, not even watch my match.
然后他就在车里睡午觉，连我的比赛都不看。

629
00:28:13.020 --> 00:28:15.280
And then after the match, I'd get in the van.
比赛结束后，我上回了车。

630
00:28:15.420 --> 00:28:16.520
He'd be like, victory or death?
他会问：不胜则死？

631
00:28:16.520 --> 00:28:19.320
And if I said death, he'd say, stinking, Kinsey.
如果我说死，他就会说：真逊啊，金西。

632
00:28:20.500 --> 00:28:21.400
Stinking, Kinsey.
真逊啊，金西。

633
00:28:21.840 --> 00:28:23.120
OK, so you have Coach Lunn.
好吧，这就是兰恩教练。

634
00:28:23.260 --> 00:28:26.080
And then the biggest tennis influence in my life is my mom.
然后对我的网球生涯影响最大的人是我妈妈。

635
00:28:26.720 --> 00:28:30.360
My mother was an amazing, amazing tennis player.
我母亲是个了不起、极其了不起的网球运动员。

636
00:28:30.540 --> 00:28:32.280
I'll never be as good as she was.
我永远也达不到她当年的水平。

637
00:28:32.760 --> 00:28:35.100
And I just grew up watching her matches.
我从小就是看着她的比赛长大的。

638
00:28:35.280 --> 00:28:39.860
And she has a very dear friend who she played tennis with, who is from the Netherlands, Karina.
她有一个非常亲密的朋友兼网球双打搭档，名叫卡丽娜，来自荷兰。

639
00:28:40.140 --> 00:28:44.800
And her and Karina would say to each other before a doubles match, stick it in their ear.
她和卡丽娜在双打比赛前会对彼此说：把球塞进他们耳朵里。

640
00:28:44.800 --> 00:28:48.840
And so my mom will say to me before a match, go stick it in their ear.
所以我妈在比赛前会对我说：去把球塞进他们耳朵里。

641
00:28:49.160 --> 00:28:52.460
When I retell the story, I have to remember to really pronunciate ear.
当我重新讲述这个故事时，我得记得把“耳朵”这个词发音重一点。

642
00:28:52.740 --> 00:28:56.280
Because for a long time, my tennis friends thought I was saying, stick it in their rear.
因为很长一段时间里，我的网球朋友们都以为我说的是：把球塞进他们屁眼里。

643
00:28:56.660 --> 00:28:57.020
OK.
好吧。

644
00:28:57.440 --> 00:28:58.280
Stick it in their rear.
把球塞进他们屁眼里。

