00:54:45.720 --> 00:54:46.960
Thanks so much for writing in.
非常感谢大家的来信。

1283
00:54:47.540 --> 00:54:53.320
Well, listen, before we go, lady, you were so generous in my birthday episode.
听着，在我们结束之前，女士，你在我的生日特别集里对我也太慷慨了。

1284
00:54:53.620 --> 00:54:57.960
You made a donation to the Library Foundation of Los Angeles in my honor.
你以我的名义向洛杉矶图书馆基金会进行了捐赠。

1285
00:54:58.180 --> 00:55:01.280
And I'd like you to know that a donation has been made in your honor.
我也想让你知道，我也以你的名义做了一笔捐赠。

1286
00:55:01.940 --> 00:55:12.380
Now, I know the charities that you already support, and I wanted to support a place that made me think of you, that I thought captured your spirit.
我了解你平时支持的那些慈善机构，而我想支持一个能让我联想到你、觉得能体现你精神的地方。

1287
00:55:12.380 --> 00:55:15.720
And I'm going to get choked up when I think about it,
一想到这儿我就有点哽咽，

1288
00:55:15.820 --> 00:55:30.380
but something about you that you have to know you to know is that you take a very active and personal advocacy role in a lot of people's lives in your life.
但关于你，有一点是必须真正了解你才能体会的，那就是你在生活中扮演着许多人的人生挚友和坚定捍卫者，你非常积极地在背后支持和保护他们。

1289
00:55:30.380 --> 00:55:42.820
Friends and family members, I experienced this when I went through my breast cancer treatment, the ways that you advocated for me and protected me in our workplace,
朋友和家人，当我经历乳腺癌治疗时，我亲身体验过你在职场上是如何为我奔走、保护我的，

1290
00:55:42.820 --> 00:55:46.340
but you do elements of this that go even further.
但你所做的其实远不止这些。

1291
00:55:46.340 --> 00:55:54.720
So, I don't want to share your personal life, but let's say, for example, you have a friend, English is their second language.
所以，我不想过多分享你的私生活，但举个例子，假设你有个朋友，英语是第二语言。

1292
00:55:55.660 --> 00:56:02.580
When that friend fell ill, you went to those doctor's appointments, and you took notes, and you called the insurance companies.
当那位朋友生病时，你会陪着去赴医生的预约，做笔记，还给保险公司打电话。

1293
00:56:03.360 --> 00:56:08.120
You did that kind of work to make sure that your friend was getting the best care.
你做了这些琐碎却重要的工作，只为了确保你的朋友能得到最好的照顾。

1294
00:56:08.900 --> 00:56:13.440
You do that for so many people in your life all the time, and it's really moving.
你一直在为生活中的那么多人默默做着这些，真的非常感人。

1295
00:56:13.440 --> 00:56:28.600
And there's an organization called CASA, and what CASA volunteers do is they are trained to work as child welfare advocates and family advocates, so they're not social workers.
有一个叫做CASA的组织，CASA的志愿者经过专门培训，可以作为儿童福利倡导者和家庭倡导者，他们不是社工。

1296
00:56:28.600 --> 00:56:37.260
It's a volunteer organization, and they kind of go beyond what a social worker is able to do because social workers are stretched so thin.
这是一个志愿者组织，他们的工作某种程度上超越了社工的能力范围，因为社工们实在分身乏术。

1297
00:56:37.260 --> 00:56:46.880
So, a CASA volunteer will get matched with a family or a child, and they advocate for them in a very personal and a direct way.
因此，CASA的志愿者会与一个家庭或儿童进行匹配，并以非常私人且直接的方式为他们发声、争取权益。

1298
00:56:47.020 --> 00:56:48.980
So, they will sit in the courtroom.
所以，他们会坐在法庭里陪同。

1299
00:56:49.100 --> 00:56:52.220
If that child needs dental care, they'll find the dentiSt.
如果那个孩子需要牙科护理，他们会帮忙找牙医。

1300
00:56:52.520 --> 00:56:57.820
They will try to get that covered however it can be covered.
无论如何，他们会想方设法争取将这些费用报销涵盖进去。

1301
00:56:57.980 --> 00:56:59.760
They support them educationally.
他们在教育上给予支持。

1302
00:56:59.760 --> 00:57:08.940
Anything having to do with their physical or mental health, their safety, their permanency goals, that's what these volunteers do.
任何与他们的身心健康、安全以及永久安置目标相关的事情，这就是这些志愿者所做的。

1303
00:57:09.380 --> 00:57:13.800
And that reminds me of you, and so a donation has been made in your name to this organization.
这让我想起了你，所以我们以你的名义向这个组织进行了一笔捐款。

1304
00:57:13.920 --> 00:57:15.280
Thank you so much, lady.
太感谢你了，女士。

1305
00:57:15.560 --> 00:57:16.940
That means so much to me.
这对我的意义太重大了。

1306
00:57:17.080 --> 00:57:18.200
It's a great organization.
这是一个很棒的组织。

1307
00:57:18.400 --> 00:57:20.860
I actually have a friend who works with them.
我其实有个朋友就在他们那里工作。

1308
00:57:20.980 --> 00:57:25.480
I didn't know that you were making a donation, but that's wonderful, and I really appreciate that.
我之前不知道你要捐款，但这太棒了，我真的很感激。

1309
00:57:25.480 --> 00:57:26.280
That's special.
这很特别。

1310
00:57:26.540 --> 00:57:34.420
You know, what are we here for if not to care for others and be kind, and, you know, we're all in this together.
你知道的，我们来这里如果不是为了关爱他人、保持善良，那是为了什么呢，而且，你知道的，我们都在这条船上。

1311
00:57:34.420 --> 00:57:35.300
We really are.
确实如此。

1312
00:57:35.760 --> 00:57:40.180
Yeah, but lady, you do, like, real high-effort work for the people you love.
对啊，但是女士，你对你爱的人会付出那种真正高精力的努力。

1313
00:57:40.460 --> 00:57:45.620
You know, you make the phone calls, you figure out the appointments, you go the extra mile.
你知道的，你会打电话、安排预约、全力以赴。

1314
00:57:45.840 --> 00:57:46.720
Well, thanks, everyone.
好的，谢谢大家。

1315
00:57:47.000 --> 00:57:49.480
Thank you so much for this birthday episode, you guys.
非常感谢你们为我制作的这个生日特辑。

1316
00:57:49.480 --> 00:57:51.000
I just have had the best time.
我刚才真的过得太开心了。

1317
00:57:51.000 --> 00:57:54.340
I left you a message on the drive-in that I was so excited.
我在开车时给你留了言，说我太激动了。

1318
00:57:54.340 --> 00:57:56.820
Well, I hope you feel celebrated.
嗯，希望你感受到了被庆祝的快乐。

1319
00:57:57.220 --> 00:58:00.040
Everyone, thank you for listening, and we love you.
大家，谢谢你们的收听，我们爱你们。

1320
00:58:00.120 --> 00:58:00.920
We'll see you next week.
我们下周见。

1321
00:58:01.080 --> 00:58:01.940
Yeah, see you then.
好，到时候见。

1322
00:58:02.280 --> 00:58:06.680
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

1323
00:58:07.000 --> 00:58:12.060
Office Ladies is a presentation of Odyssey and is produced by Jenna Fisher and Angela Kinsey.
《办公室女士》是由奥德赛呈现，由珍娜·费舍尔和安吉拉·金西制作的。

1324
00:58:12.260 --> 00:58:16.480
Our senior producer is Matt Beagle, and our audio engineer is Sam Kiefer.
我们的资深制作人是马特·比格尔，我们的音频工程师是萨姆·基弗。

1325
00:58:16.760 --> 00:58:19.320
Odyssey's executive producer is Leah Reese Dennis.
奥德赛的执行制作人是莉亚·里斯·丹尼斯。

1326
